      "message": "In `prepare_dut()`, `c2d2` uses `gsc_ec_reset` instead of `cold_reset` to reset the EC (line 254). Should we also check for `c2d2` here and pulse `gsc_ec_reset` to ensure the EC reboots properly? Or just always use gsc_ec_reset and never use cold_reset?\n\n```python\n        controller \u003d self._get_controller()\n        if controller \u003d\u003d \"ccd\":\n            logger.info(\"Deasserting sysrst on CCD...\")\n            # ...\n        elif controller \u003d\u003d \"c2d2\":\n            self.servo.set_many([(\"gsc_ec_reset\", \"on\"), (\"gsc_ec_reset\", \"off\")])\n        else:\n            self.servo.set_many([(\"cold_reset\", \"on\"), (\"cold_reset\", \"off\")])\n```",
